From 1250320cbe568b92ca81791b362b642dec975ff9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hardening <hardening@example.invalid>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 08:25:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 7/9] webui: add ETag + gzip + immutable caching to the
 embedded SPA handler

The embedded Next export ships ~1.55 MB of JS/CSS. Files read from embed.FS
report a zero modtime, so http.ServeFileFS emitted no Last-Modified and nothing
set an ETag: the browser had no validator and re-downloaded the whole bundle on
every page load. The handler also ignored Accept-Encoding, so those bytes went
out uncompressed.

Measured from a 211 ms-RTT link: 17 assets / 1,554,053 B, 8.57 s serialised,
1.98 s at 6-way parallelism, 0.28 MB/s per SSH stream.

Now each asset is digested (sha256, 16 bytes, quoted strong ETag) and, for
compressible types over 1 KiB, gzipped once at BestCompression and cached in
memory (~450 KB total). Responses carry Vary: Accept-Encoding and honour
gzip;q=0. /_next/static/* gets public, max-age=31536000, immutable because
Next content-hashes those filenames; HTML gets no-cache so a rebuild is never
served stale. Range and HEAD still work (http.ServeContent underneath).

Stdlib only, no new module dependencies.
